.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1128 AM PDT Sun Sep 27 2026

High clouds continue to stream in across the region revealing an
dissipating marine layer beneath. While stratus persist along the
coast, inland locations are rapidly scattering out. An
approaching trough will deepen the marine layer tonight into
Monday with a return of low clouds expected once again tonight
into Monday morning.

Vicinity of SFO...MVFR conditions will quickly scatter out making
way for VFR conditions with scattered high clouds. Moderate
confidence that MVFR cigs will return overnight between 06z-09z.
Light to moderate onshore flow will prevail through midday with
moderate and gusty winds expected this afternoon for KSFO.
Clearing is anticipated around 17z Monday morning.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...MVFR conditions will quickly scatter out
making way for VFR conditions with scattered high clouds. Moderate
to high confidence that MVFR cigs will return this evening around
02z. Light to locally moderate onshore flow is prevail.

