.MARINE...
(Today through Friday)
Issued at 902 AM PDT Sun Sep 27 2026

Moderate north winds will persist today, becoming moderate to
strong as we head into Monday. Strongest winds will be over
northern outer water and south of Point Pinos with near gale force
gusts expected at times. Winds hold through midweek then taper
becoming light to moderate by the end of the work week. Tropical
activity will produce long period southerly swell by the middle of
the week.

